In the initial prototype, the scissor arms were fabricated from 1/4-inch laser-cut acrylic. The hydraulic system consisted of PVC components, a resin 3D-printed piston seal, and an O-ring for sealing. A commercially sourced relief valve was integrated, and the hydraulic mechanism was positioned beneath the lift platform, with an external piston used for manual force input. The prototype weighed approximately 12 lbs and was capable of lifting loads up to 50 lbs.

