Several challenges arose during development, primarily due to material and budget constraints. With a $250 budget limit, PVC was the primary machinable material available, and manufacturing labor was also factored into material choices. As a result, the hydraulic system was not fully sealed, leading to leakage and an inability to maintain sufficient pressure, which limited lift height to only a few inches. Additionally, fabrication with thicker plywood proved difficult without access to laser cutting, requiring manual cutting and sanding processes that reduced dimensional accuracy and tolerances.




